{"kind":"artifact","text":"ui at 94f2d8f592a83882483a874cc75b75ecb385d7d6 (branch request/needs-action-ratification): the board now shows the ratification queue.\n\nSelf-initiated work, on hugh's authorization of 2026-08-22 to carry the substance of retired request 4c739023 forward without a self-request. This artifact is the implementation report.\n\nWhat changed. workRows iterates projection.commitments, and ratification is not a commitment, so the one duty only a ratifier can discharge was the population the board could not display. It was being found by being told in conversation, which is not a queue. ratificationRows adds it as a population beside the commitments, reached from its own count like the two summary lines already there, and never added into a figure with them: they are owed by different people for different reasons.\n\nWhich kinds are owed is read from the vocabulary rather than listed in the UI. A kind is owed when its satisfier names the ratifier role and it does not render as a note. An assert names that role too, but stands on its author's signature and has already done its job unratified, so counting the 403 of them would bury the 15 that are genuinely inert without force. Measured against this log the queue is 15: propose=14, roster=1. Reading the vocabulary also picks up admission-profile, infra-key, kind-def and seal, none of which a hand-written list would have carried - which is the condition doing real work rather than being satisfied on paper.\n\nWhere the room has no ratifier, or more than one, the queue names nobody rather than guessing, and the screen says which case it is. An empty waits-on column would otherwise read as nothing owed, which is the shape of the original defect one level down.\n\nTwo conditions in the retired request no longer describe the code. WorkDrawer.tsx, workItemNeedsAction and needsCount are gone, and with them both the me-resolution and the summing-over-topics defects: the current list has no per-viewer filter and no topic sum. The surviving structural gap is the commitments-only iteration, and that is what this head fixes. The topic condition is still pinned by a test - a proposal belonging to no commitment and no thread appears - so a future reintroduction of topic summing cannot silently drop it.\n\nTests and gates actually run at this head. npx tsc --noEmit clean. npm test 68 pass, 0 fail, including five new tests in ui/test/ratification.test.mjs and an extension of the dom.test.mjs invariant that each number opens to exactly its own rows. Green was not taken on trust: five mutations of the seam were each caught - counting note-rendered kinds, guessing a ratifier when several or none hold the role, keeping ratified rows, counting fold-refused acts, and making the population open to nothing.\n\nNot yet run at this head: the Go gates, which this change does not touch (no Go file is modified).\n\nOne thing for the reviewer and for whoever merges next. The path ui already carries two live artifacts: 3d89c5e0 (mine, commit 33c29b1e, in main) and a944f670 (planner's, commit 39fc1720, branch request/thread-record-detail, not in main and carrying no review request). This artifact is a third candidate at that path. Whoever merges first must retire the others, and I cannot retire planner's. That ordering needs settling before any merge here, not after.","body":{"commit":"94f2d8f592a83882483a874cc75b75ecb385d7d6","path":"ui"}}